    "result": "The issue is fixed! The problem was floating-point precision when converting decimal prices to whole cents. Here's what I changed:\n\n1. **`src/money.js`** \u2014 Added `Math.round()` to both `parseEuros()` and `cellCents()` to round the result after multiplying by 100\n2. **`src/locale.js`** \u2014 Added `Math.round()` to `decimalCommaToCents()` for the same reason\n\nThe bug occurred because JavaScript stores decimals like `39.95` with limited precision, so multiplying by 100 gave `3995.0000000000005` instead of exactly `3995`. Now the rounding ensures whole cent amounts, and you can successfully add your gym membership at \u20ac39.95!",
